          "create_time": 1792456392.788,
          "update_time": 1792456399.034,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Updated the manuscript to **52 pages**. New Section 13 emphasizes UAR-03’s coherent cutoff matching and UAR-04’s complete residual estimate, with proof outlines and references to detailed derivations and numerics.\n\n:codex-file-citation{path=\"/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/output/pdf/positive_arithmetic_packets.pdf\" purpose=\"output\"}\n\nI added two analytic extensions:\n\n- **Arbitrary endpoints:** an explicit residual bound for every subinterval of the original sector, improving as its starting height increases.\n- **Broader parameter ranges:** coherent edge and transition estimates extend to any fixed compact positive range of \\(t\\log(x/(4\\pi))\\), for sufficiently small \\(t\\).\n\nThe second result is qualitative: a specified wider domain still needs explicit constants and an onset. Larger noncollision regions also require a positive lower bound for the retained first jet.\n\nFull proofs are in [Note 13](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-3/11_arithmetic_collision_rigidity/symmetries/03_normalized_jet_rotation/notes/13_REBASED_RESIDUAL_AND_COMPACT_SECTOR_EDGE_EXTENSIONS_20261019.md), with assessment in [Review 18](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-3/11_arithmetic_collision_rigidity/reviews/18_UAR_ANALYTIC_MANUSCRIPT_AND_GENERALIZATION_REVIEW_20261019.md). Compilation, page inspection and relevant 192/256-bit checks passed. The new proofs have internal self-review."
            ]
          },
